--TEST--
A `<?nvs` tag inside an html template is `E0010`, reported once per tag with the two replacements named, and is then text — `rule:core-classes/html-template`, ADR 0202
--FILE--
<?nvs
echo html`<ul><?nvs echo 1; ?><li></li><?nvs ?></ul>`;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0010]: a code block cannot open inside an html template
  --> %s:2:15
  |
2 | echo html`<ul><?nvs echo 1; ?><li></li><?nvs ?></ul>`;
  |               ^^^^^ an html template is one expression
  = help: write `<?= expr ?>` for one value, or build the fragments in code mode and compose them with `+` or `Core\Html::join`

error[E0010]: a code block cannot open inside an html template
  --> %s:2:40
  |
2 | echo html`<ul><?nvs echo 1; ?><li></li><?nvs ?></ul>`;
  |                                        ^^^^^ an html template is one expression
  = help: write `<?= expr ?>` for one value, or build the fragments in code mode and compose them with `+` or `Core\Html::join`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
